dzn: Offer VK_EXT_queue_family_foreign

Venus passes VK_EXT_queue_family_foreign through from the host driver, and
Dawn, Chrome's Graphite backend, counts VK_ANDROID_external_memory_android_
hardware_buffer only when the device also has it. Under WSL2 the guest's
Venus device therefore had hardware buffers but Dawn did not, so Dawn
lacked YCbCrVulkanSamplers, which Chrome requires on Android: Chromium's GPU
process failed to create its Dawn device and Chromium exited at every start
("GPU process isn't usable").

Dozen already treats a barrier to or from any queue family other than the
command pool's as an ownership transfer, moving the image to or from
D3D12_BARRIER_LAYOUT_COMMON, the layout D3D12 requires of a resource shared
with another device or process; the legacy barrier path ignores queue
families. VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_FOREIGN_EXT takes that path as
VK_QUEUE_FAMILY_EXTERNAL does, so offering the extension needs no other
change.

diff --git a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_device.c b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_device.c
index 67dcfdb..7dce5ae 100644
--- a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_device.c
+++ b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_device.c
@@ -176,6 +176,7 @@ dzn_physical_device_get_extensions(struct dzn_physical_device *pdev)
       .EXT_pipeline_creation_cache_control   = true,
       .EXT_pipeline_creation_feedback        = true,
       .EXT_private_data                      = true,
+      .EXT_queue_family_foreign              = true,
       .EXT_tooling_info                      = true,
       .MSFT_layered_driver                   = true,
    };
